:root {
  --ink: #f4ead7;
  --paper: #f7f0df;
  --muted: #b9ab97;
  --gold: #e8c57a;
  --gold-deep: #b9873d;
  --crimson: #b7333c;
  --crimson-deep: #671923;
  --night: #08060d;
  --panel: rgba(9, 7, 15, 0.84);
  --line: rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.3);
  --pixel: "Courier New", "Lucida Console", monospace;
  --serif: "Hiragino Mincho ProN", "Yu Mincho", "Times New Roman", serif;
}

* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

html,
body {
  margin: 0;
  min-height: 100%;
  background: #050409;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: var(--pixel);
}

body {
  min-height: 100vh;
  min-height: 100svh;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  overflow: hidden;
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 42%, rgba(70, 34, 55, 0.32), transparent 56%),
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 110%, rgba(114, 50, 38, 0.2), transparent 52%),
    repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.012) 0 1px, transparent 1px 3px),
    #050409;
  user-select: none;
  -webkit-user-select: none;
  -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
}

button {
  font: inherit;
  color: inherit;
}

#app {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 14px;
  padding: 20px;
}

#frame {
  position: relative;
  width: min(1280px, calc(100vw - 40px), calc((100vh - 92px) * 16 / 9));
  aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
  background: #07060c;
  border: 1px solid rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.35);
  box-shadow:
    0 0 0 1px #23160f,
    0 0 0 5px rgba(9, 7, 13, 0.8),
    0 24px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.78),
    0 0 80px rgba(127, 33, 43, 0.14);
  overflow: hidden;
  touch-action: none;
}

#frame::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 7;
  pointer-events: none;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 244, 219, 0.07);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.48);
}

#game {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  image-rendering: pixelated;
  image-rendering: crisp-edges;
  background: #08060d;
}

.screen-fx {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 6;
}

.scanlines {
  opacity: 0.16;
  background: repeating-linear-gradient(
    0deg,
    rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5) 0,
    rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5) 1px,
    transparent 1px,
    transparent 3px
  );
  mix-blend-mode: multiply;
}

.vignette {
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse at center, transparent 52%, rgba(3, 2, 6, 0.36) 80%, rgba(3, 2, 6, 0.72) 100%),
    linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2), transparent 14%, transparent 84%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35));
}

.screen {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 10;
}

.hidden {
  display: none !important;
}

.title-screen {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding: clamp(14px, 4vw, 58px);
  background:
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(5, 3, 9, 0.94) 0%, rgba(5, 3, 9, 0.72) 34%, rgba(5, 3, 9, 0.08) 68%, transparent 100%),
    linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(5, 3, 9, 0.62), transparent 45%);
}

.title-panel {
  width: min(480px, 62%);
  position: relative;
  animation: title-in 900ms cubic-bezier(0.19, 1, 0.22, 1) both;
}

@keyframes title-in {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(14px); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
}

.seal {
  position: absolute;
  top: -8px;
  right: 8%;
  width: clamp(38px, 5vw, 58px);
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  color: #f7e5cd;
  background: #a12630;
  border: 2px solid #d76065;
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: clamp(22px, 3.2vw, 36px);
  font-weight: 700;
  transform: rotate(6deg);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(118, 25, 34, 0.4), 0 8px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
  opacity: 0.94;
}

.eyebrow {
  margin: 0 0 8px;
  color: var(--gold);
  font-size: clamp(7px, 0.82vw, 11px);
  letter-spacing: 0.3em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  font-weight: 700;
}

.logo {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: "Arial Black", Impact, sans-serif;
  font-size: clamp(42px, 7.3vw, 100px);
  line-height: 0.8;
  letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  color: #f8efde;
  text-shadow:
    3px 3px 0 #7d2029,
    6px 6px 0 rgba(34, 8, 13, 0.9),
    8px 10px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35),
    0 0 36px rgba(224, 159, 92, 0.15);
}

.logo span {
  display: block;
  color: #e8c57a;
  margin-left: 0.72em;
  font-size: 1.02em;
  text-shadow:
    3px 3px 0 #6e2b22,
    6px 6px 0 rgba(34, 8, 13, 0.9),
    8px 10px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
}

.jp-title {
  margin: 13px 0 0;
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: clamp(13px, 1.7vw, 23px);
  letter-spacing: 0.24em;
  color: #d8c4a5;
  opacity: 0.8;
}

.tagline {
  margin: 7px 0 19px;
  color: #9f8d78;
  font-size: clamp(8px, 0.92vw, 12px);
  letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.pixel-button {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-width: 150px;
  padding: 12px 21px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.46);
  background: rgba(26, 20, 25, 0.9);
  color: #e8ddcb;
  font-family: var(--pixel);
  font-size: clamp(9px, 1.02vw, 13px);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  cursor: pointer;
  box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
  transition: background 130ms ease, border-color 130ms ease, transform 90ms ease, color 130ms ease;
}

.pixel-button::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 3px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045);
  pointer-events: none;
}

.pixel-button:hover {
  background: rgba(62, 31, 35, 0.95);
  border-color: rgba(238, 206, 139, 0.85);
  color: #fff5df;
}

.pixel-button:active {
  transform: translate(2px, 2px);
  box-shadow: 1px 1px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
}

.pixel-button.primary {
  border-color: #c0474f;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #a52d39, #791d29);
  color: #fff0df;
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 214, 174, 0.12),
    3px 3px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6),
    0 0 30px rgba(171, 45, 57, 0.18);
}

.pixel-button.primary:hover {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #bb3744, #8a222f);
  border-color: #e58c8f;
}

#startBtn {
  width: min(290px, 94%);
  margin-bottom: 18px;
  animation: breathe 3.2s ease-in-out infinite;
}

@keyframes breathe {
  0%, 100% { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 214, 174, 0.1), 3px 3px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6), 0 0 22px rgba(171, 45, 57, 0.12); }
  50% { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 214, 174, 0.18), 3px 3px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6), 0 0 38px rgba(203, 64, 76, 0.28); }
}

.controls-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 6px;
  width: min(510px, 100%);
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

.control-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 5px;
  padding: 7px 3px 6px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(214, 192, 154, 0.13);
  background: rgba(9, 7, 12, 0.52);
}

.control-card .keys {
  display: flex;
  gap: 2px;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: 18px;
}

.control-card kbd,
kbd {
  display: inline-block;
  min-width: 17px;
  padding: 2px 4px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.34);
  border-bottom-color: rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.55);
  background: rgba(37, 30, 27, 0.9);
  color: #f0e2c8;
  font-family: var(--pixel);
  font-size: clamp(7px, 0.78vw, 10px);
  line-height: 1.2;
  text-align: center;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
}

.control-card span {
  color: #a69680;
  font-size: clamp(6px, 0.66vw, 9px);
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
}

.control-card.accent {
  border-color: rgba(89, 189, 189, 0.35);
  background: rgba(10, 29, 31, 0.5);
}

.control-card.accent span {
  color: #78c7c2;
}

.tip {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin: 0 0 9px;
  color: #8f806e;
  font-size: clamp(7px, 0.76vw, 10px);
  letter-spacing: 0.07em;
}

.glint-dot,
.red-dot {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 7px;
  height: 7px;
  transform: rotate(45deg);
}

.glint-dot {
  background: #e8eee9;
  box-shadow: 0 0 8px #b9ffff;
}

.red-dot {
  background: #cb3946;
  box-shadow: 0 0 8px #ff5964;
}

.best {
  margin: 0;
  color: #8e7d68;
  font-size: clamp(7px, 0.72vw, 10px);
  letter-spacing: 0.2em;
}

.best span {
  color: var(--gold);
}

.credit {
  position: absolute;
  right: clamp(16px, 3vw, 42px);
  bottom: clamp(12px, 2.4vw, 30px);
  margin: 0;
  color: rgba(222, 196, 156, 0.45);
  font-size: clamp(6px, 0.7vw, 9px);
  letter-spacing: 0.3em;
}

.overlay {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  padding: 18px;
  background: rgba(4, 3, 8, 0.62);
  backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
}

.dialog {
  width: min(520px, 94%);
  padding: clamp(18px, 3vw, 38px);
  text-align: center;
  border: 1px solid rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.3);
  background:
    linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(25, 18, 24, 0.97), rgba(9, 7, 13, 0.97));
  box-shadow:
    0 0 0 4px rgba(8, 6, 11, 0.8),
    0 0 0 5px rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.12),
    0 30px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
  animation: dialog-in 260ms ease-out both;
}

@keyframes dialog-in {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.97) translateY(8px); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1) translateY(0); }
}

.dialog h2 {
  margin: 6px 0 5px;
  font-family: "Arial Black", Impact, sans-serif;
  font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 64px);
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  color: #f4e8d3;
  text-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #6f2029, 0 0 28px rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.15);
}

.dialog .eyebrow {
  margin-bottom: 5px;
}

.end-message {
  margin: 0 auto 16px;
  max-width: 360px;
  color: #a3937f;
  font-size: clamp(8px, 0.9vw, 11px);
  line-height: 1.7;
}

.pause-controls {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 8px 14px;
  margin: 18px auto 20px;
  max-width: 410px;
  color: #a89883;
  font-size: clamp(8px, 0.86vw, 11px);
}

.pause-controls p {
  margin: 0;
}

.button-row {
  display: flex;
  gap: 10px;
  justify-content: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.dialog-note {
  margin: 16px 0 0;
  color: #7f715f;
  font-size: clamp(7px, 0.74vw, 10px);
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}

.dialog-note kbd {
  font-size: 8px;
  padding: 1px 4px;
}

.stats {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
  gap: 1px;
  margin: 18px 0 22px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.16);
  background: rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.13);
}

.stats div {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 6px;
  padding: 10px 3px;
  background: rgba(8, 6, 12, 0.94);
}

.stats span {
  color: #7f715f;
  font-size: clamp(5px, 0.62vw, 8px);
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
}

.stats strong {
  color: #e8c57a;
  font-size: clamp(12px, 1.5vw, 19px);
  font-weight: 700;
}

.icon-button {
  position: absolute;
  top: 10px;
  right: 10px;
  z-index: 20;
  width: 29px;
  height: 29px;
  padding: 0;
  border: 1px solid rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.24);
  background: rgba(8, 6, 12, 0.58);
  color: #c5b18e;
  font-size: 14px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color 120ms ease, color 120ms ease;
}

.icon-button:hover {
  border-color: rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.6);
  color: #f5e5c6;
}

.outside-note {
  margin: 0;
  color: rgba(190, 172, 144, 0.38);
  font-size: 10px;
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  text-align: center;
}

/* Touch controls */
.touch-controls {
  position: absolute;
  inset: auto 0 0 0;
  z-index: 15;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: flex-end;
  padding: 10px clamp(10px, 2vw, 22px) clamp(10px, 2vw, 20px);
  pointer-events: none;
}

.touch-cluster {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
  gap: clamp(5px, 1.1vw, 10px);
  pointer-events: auto;
}

.touch-btn {
  width: clamp(42px, 7.2vw, 66px);
  height: clamp(42px, 7.2vw, 66px);
  border: 1px solid rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.32);
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: rgba(10, 8, 14, 0.47);
  color: rgba(245, 234, 214, 0.82);
  font-family: var(--pixel);
  font-size: clamp(8px, 1.2vw, 11px);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 1px;
  touch-action: none;
  backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
  transition: background 80ms ease, transform 80ms ease, border-color 80ms ease;
}

.touch-btn span {
  color: rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.55);
  font-size: clamp(5px, 0.7vw, 7px);
}

.touch-btn.active,
.touch-btn:active {
  background: rgba(144, 42, 50, 0.7);
  border-color: #e5aa7a;
  transform: scale(0.94);
}

.touch-btn.jump {
  background: rgba(22, 37, 36, 0.5);
  border-color: rgba(119, 196, 184, 0.28);
}

.touch-btn.parry {
  border-color: rgba(108, 198, 204, 0.55);
  background: rgba(11, 43, 45, 0.58);
  width: clamp(50px, 8.5vw, 76px);
  height: clamp(50px, 8.5vw, 76px);
}

.touch-btn.attack {
  border-color: rgba(214, 115, 92, 0.5);
  background: rgba(63, 18, 22, 0.55);
  width: clamp(54px, 9.3vw, 82px);
  height: clamp(54px, 9.3vw, 82px);
}

.touch-btn.dodge {
  background: rgba(35, 30, 49, 0.55);
  border-color: rgba(175, 158, 205, 0.4);
}

.rotate-hint {
  position: absolute;
  top: 10px;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translateX(-50%);
  z-index: 22;
  padding: 5px 10px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(232, 197, 122, 0.2);
  background: rgba(8, 6, 12, 0.74);
  color: #b9a587;
  font-size: 8px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  white-space: nowrap;
  pointer-events: none;
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  #app {
    padding: 8px;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  #frame {
    width: min(100vw - 16px, calc((100svh - 42px) * 16 / 9));
  }

  .title-panel {
    width: min(430px, 68%);
  }

  .controls-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    width: min(330px, 100%);
  }

  .control-card {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 7px;
    padding: 5px 4px;
  }

  .control-card .keys {
    min-height: 16px;
  }

  .outside-note {
    display: none;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 640px), (orientation: portrait) {
  #frame {
    width: 100vw;
    max-height: 100svh;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    border-width: 0;
    box-shadow: none;
  }

  #app {
    padding: 0;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .title-screen {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(5, 3, 9, 0.93), rgba(5, 3, 9, 0.74) 52%, rgba(5, 3, 9, 0.16)),
      linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(5, 3, 9, 0.72), transparent 45%);
  }

  .title-panel {
    width: min(360px, 72%);
  }

  .seal {
    right: 3%;
    top: -2px;
    width: 32px;
    font-size: 20px;
  }

  .logo {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 10.2vw, 55px);
  }

  .tagline {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .controls-grid {
    display: none;
  }

  .tip {
    max-width: 260px;
    margin-bottom: 7px;
  }

  .credit {
    display: none;
  }

  #startBtn {
    margin-bottom: 9px;
    min-width: 190px;
    padding: 9px 14px;
  }

  .pause-controls {
    display: none;
  }

  .dialog {
    padding: 16px 18px;
  }

  .stats {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    margin: 11px 0 14px;
  }

  .stats div:nth-child(4),
  .stats div:nth-child(5) {
    display: none;
  }

  .dialog-note {
    display: none;
  }
}

@media (orientation: portrait) and (max-width: 700px) {
  .rotate-hint:not(.hidden) {
    display: block;
  }
}

@media (max-height: 470px) and (orientation: landscape) {
  #app {
    padding: 0;
  }

  #frame {
    width: min(100vw, calc(100svh * 16 / 9));
    border-width: 0;
    box-shadow: none;
  }

  .title-screen {
    padding: 10px 26px;
  }

  .title-panel {
    width: min(460px, 62%);
  }

  .logo {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 8vh, 58px);
  }

  .jp-title {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .tagline {
    margin: 3px 0 10px;
  }

  .controls-grid {
    margin-bottom: 7px;
  }

  .control-card {
    padding: 4px 2px;
  }

  .tip {
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }

  #startBtn {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    padding: 8px 14px;
  }

  .outside-note {
    display: none;
  }
}

@media (hover: none) and (pointer: coarse) {
  .outside-note {
    display: none;
  }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *,
  *::before,
  *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.001ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.001ms !important;
  }
}

content.text:
Now game.js. This is the big one. Let me carefully architect and write.

Let's define all code in module.

Outline:

```js
// ===== constants/helpers
const VW=640,VH=360,GROUND=298,WORLD_W=1060;
const canvas=document.getElementById('game'), ctx=...
ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled=false;

const $ = id => document.getElementById(id)
...
// DOM refs
// persistent
const store = {get/set}

// AudioEngine
class Sound { ... }
const sound = new Sound();

// Input
const input = new Input();

// Game data constants KINDS, WAVES, PLAYER_ATTACKS, ENEMY_ATTACKS
```

Audio details: Need reliable and not annoying. Implement `Sound` with:
- `ctx`, `master`, `musicGain`, `sfxGain`, `muted` from localStorage.
- `init()` creates context, master gain .45, music gain .18, noise buffer.
- `resume()`.
- `tone({freq, dur, type, gain, when, slide, filter})` helper.
- `noise({dur, gain, filterFreq, q, when})`.
- SFX:
  - swing: filtered noise bandpass 1200 sweep down, short
  - hit: noise lowpass + sine 70->40
  - parry: three metallic sine/triangle 1200,1800,2400 with fast decay + noise highpass; maybe osc frequencies.
  - block: lower clang.
  - dodge: noise bandpass 400->1000
  - jump: soft
  - death: low slide
  - wave: gong (low sine + noise)
  - victory: notes
  - enemyParry: metallic.
  - step? no.
- Music scheduler: `update(now)`: if ctx and !muted, schedule next notes based on this.nextNoteTime vs ctx.currentTime. Use patterns. Maybe drones created once. `startMusic()` creates two oscillators through lowpass, gain .02; schedule koto plucks and taiko.
- Need avoid scheduling when paused? Can lower music gain while paused. Simpler music runs continuously after start. Provide mute.
- `setMuted` toggles master gain with ramp. Update icon.
- On title before start, no audio until user starts. `start()` called after user gesture; init.
- For iOS, resume on touch.

Music loop: 
```
this.step=0; this.nextTime=ctx.currentTime+0.2;
update() {
 if (!ctx||muted) return;
 while(this.nextTime < ctx.currentTime+0.2) {
   this.playStep(this.step, this.nextTime);
   this.nextTime += 0.42;
   this.step++;
 }
}
playStep(step,t) {
 const chord=[146.83,174.61,220,293.66]? pentatonic A minor.
 if (step%8===0) taiko...
 if ([0,2,4,5,7].includes(step%8)) pluck random root from [220,261.63,293.66,329.63,392]
}
```
Koto pluck: triangle + sine with fast decay, maybe two detuned. Keep volume low (0.03). Taiko: low sine 55 with pitch drop plus noise. Ambient wind? Maybe noise loop with filter, gain .01.

For parry clang use oscillator frequencies 880, 1320, 1980 randomized, delay 0.0; highpass noise. Good.

Input class:
```
class Input {
 constructor() {
   this.keys=new Set(); this.just=new Set(); this.virtual=new Set(); this.vjust=new Set()
   this.bind()
 }
 bind(){
  addEventListener('keydown', e => { if (this.isGameKey(e.code)) e.preventDefault(); if (!e.repeat) {this.keys.add(e.code); this.just.add(e.code)} });
  keyup...
  blur...
 }
 isGameKey(code) { ...}
 down(action) { KEYMAP[action].some(c => keys.has(c) || virtual...) }
 pressed(action) { if virtualPressed has action return true; map code just; }
 endFrame(){this.just.clear();this.vjust.clear()}
 setVirtual(action,on){...}
}
```
For virtual actions, map same action names. `down` checks `this.virtual.has(action)`, `pressed` checks `this.virtualPressed`. Keyboard map codes -> action.
- For Enter start etc, we use DOM listeners separately, but input can handle. Use `endFrame` at very end of RAF.

Gamepad: implement within Input:
```
pollGamepad() {
 const pads=navigator.getGamepads?.()...
 const map...
 this.gamepad = state...
 // edges for attack/parry/dodge/jump, axes left/right
}
```
Could integrate action `down` with gp. But simpler create methods:
`gpDown(action)`, `gpPressed(action)` updated each frame. Map: axes<-.35 left, >.35 right, buttons 0 jump, 2 attack, 3 parry, 1 dodge, 9 pause. Dpad 14/15. Maintain prev array. On poll, set `gp` object and `gpJust` set. `pressed` merges.
- Poll once per frame at start.
- Need poll before update. In main loop call input.pollGamepad().
- Start via gamepad? Title maybe start if Start pressed; implement.

Now entities.

Constants:
```
const PLAYER_ATTACKS = [
 {name:'slash1', windup:.07, active:.09, recover:.16, damage:10, range:58, height:38, posture:9, knock:85, lunge:110, hurt:.2, heavy:false, sfx:'swing', trail:'wide'},
 ...
]
```
Total = windup+active+recover.

Enemy attack builder: `getEnemyAttack(kind, index, phase2)`. For enemy combo:
- For ronin, choose attack variant based on `this.attackPattern` and `comboStep`. Use arrays per kind:
```
ENEMY_MOVES = {
 ronin: [
  {windup:.42, active:.1, recover:.4, damage:11, range:68, height:40, lunge:80, posture:12, unblockable:false, hurt:.25},
  {windup:.3, active:.09, recover:.5, damage:12, range:72, lunge:100...},
  {windup:.66, active:.12, recover:.65, damage:20, range:78, lunge:90, unblockable:true, hurt:.4}
 ],
 ...
}
```
But combo chaining for enemies: On start attack, choose move. On end, maybe if combo step < pattern length and rng -> next attack after short delay? Could implement `this.comboLeft` and pattern. For boss specifically. For ronin/ninja maybe 2-hit combos. When starting attack, pick pattern array and index. At end, if comboStep<pattern.length-1 and rng < .55 and player in range, start next after .1? That makes combos. But each move's windup telegraph separate. Fine.
- Simpler: `this.attackPattern = pickPattern(kind, dist)`, `this.comboStep=0`; start attack with pattern[0]; on end, if comboStep<pattern.length-1 and `this.comboChainChance` roll, after 0.08 delay start next. Need a `chainDelay` state. Could just immediately start next move at end; total recovery included in previous move, giving rhythm. For player to parry each hit, okay.
- But for normal enemies, keep mostly single attacks. Boss 3-hit combos.
- Choose boss pattern alternating:
  - pattern A: two quick slashes, third red overhead.
  - pattern B: red lunge single.
- Boss phase 2 adds more.

Enemy attack data must be cloned with phase2 scaling.

Attack data object includes `index`, `name`, `unblockable`, `range` etc.

AI:
`Fighter.updateAI(dt, game)` called before `update` maybe. It sets `moveIntent`, triggers actions. Ensure only if `game.state==='playing'` and not waveIntro? enemies can act after spawnT.
Pseudo:
```
updateAI(dt, game) {
 if (dead/stagger/hurt/attack/parry/dodge || spawnT>0) { this.moveIntent=0; return; }
 const p=game.player; if p.dead return
 const dx=p.x-this.x, adx=abs(dx), dir=dx<0?-1:1;
 if (adx>10) this.facing=dir;
 this.aiTimer-=dt; this.aiDecideTimer-=dt;
 // face and move
 let want=0;
 if (adx>this.preferredRange) want=dir;
 else if (adx<30) want=-dir*0.6;
 else want=0;
 // jump over sometimes
 if (this.jumpCd<=0 && ((adx<34 && Math.random()<dt*1.2) || (adx>170 && Math.random()<dt*.4))) { this.jump(dir); this.jumpCd=2.5+rand; }
 // separation
 ...
 this.moveIntent=want;
 if (this.aiDecideTimer<=0) {
   this.aiDecideTimer = 0.09+Math.random()*0.12;
   this.decideCombat(game,p,adx,dir);
 }
}
```
Defensive reaction should check player's attack windup. `decideCombat`:
```
const pAttack=p.state==='attack'?p.attack:null;
if (pAttack && adx < 108) {
 const inWindup = p.stateT < pAttack.windup+0.06;
 if (inWindup) {
   if (this.parryCd<=0 && adx<92 && rand()<this.stats.parryChance) { this.startParry(game); return; }
   if (this.dodgeCd<=0 && rand()<this.stats.dodgeChance) { this.startDodge(this.pickDodgeDir(p,dir), game); return; }
 }
 // if active and dodge available, lower chance
}
```
- Avoid reacting to player's third attack? no.
- Attack:
```
if (this.attackCd<=0 && adx < this.reach+12 && Math.abs(p.y-this.y)<26 && game.canEnemyAttack(this)) {
  if (Math.random()<this.stats.aggression) { this.startEnemyCombo(game, dist); return; }
}
```
- Pacing: attackCd set after attack ends to random range; start cooldown maybe.
- If player far, don't attack; approach.
- For boss with phase2 stats.

`game.canEnemyAttack` counts enemies currently attacking: return count < (game.enemies.length>1?1:2) or rng<0.2. Boss always. Maybe allow 2 simultaneous if 3 enemies. We only have max 2 alive except maybe boss. Implement at most 1 attacker unless boss.
- But if enemy state attack currently, it's the token. Others wait. Good.

`startParry`: sets state, parry window, cd 2-5s. Enemy parry can happen while player winds up; if player delays, enemy parry ends before hit and is vulnerable. Good.

`startDodge(dir)`: enemy dodge direction choose away or through (toward) with i-frames. If near wall, choose inward. Also if adx small, through. Set dodgeCd.
- Enemy jumping: jump method with direction; mark jumpCd.

Player actions:
`game.updatePlayer` or `Fighter` methods.

Fighter `requestAttack`:
```
requestAttack(game) {
 if (!this.canAct() || !this.onGround) return;
 if (this.state==='attack') { if (this.stateT > this.attack.windup) this.bufferedAttack=true; return; }
 let idx = 0;
 if (this.comboWindow>0) idx = Math.min(this.attackIndex+1, 2);
 this.startAttack(idx,game)
}
```
`canAct` = state in idle/run and !dead and onGround? For attack/parry/dodge requires ground. Jump allows at start.
- If state === 'jump' and onGround false → can't attack. Once land sets idle.
- `requestParry`: canAct && onGround.
- `requestDodge`: canAct (or maybe jump? no) and onGround.
- `jump`: canAct && onGround; sets state 'jump', onGround=false, vy=-jumpPower, vx=moveIntent*...; sfx.
- Need cooldown parry/dodge update even when busy.

`startAttack`:
- Determine attack object `this.isPlayer ? PLAYER_ATTACKS[idx] : ...`.
- Face nearest target automatically? For player, if there is living enemy within 110, face nearest; also if attack pressed while moving maybe face nearest. Do automatically for combos. For enemies auto face player.
- set state, stateT=0, attackIndex, attack = data, hitSet.clear, buffered false; vx = facing*lunge; comboWindow=0; sound swing? Play at active maybe; set `swingPlayed=false` and play when active.
- `this.attackTotal`.
- If player third, heavier screen.

`updateAttack(dt, game)`:
```
const a=this.attack
if (!this.swingPlayed && stateT >= a.windup) {game.sound.swing(...); this.swingPlayed=true}
if (stateT >= a.windup && stateT <= a.windup+a.active) this.performHits(game)
// friction
this.vx = approach(this.vx, 0, (this.stateT>a.windup+a.active?900:320)*dt)
if (stateT >= total) {
  this.attackIndex = ...; this.comboWindow = 0.42
  if (this.bufferedAttack && this.attackIndex<2 && this.isPlayer) { this.bufferedAttack=false; this.startAttack(this.attackIndex+1, game, true) }
  else if (this.enemyComboLeft>0) { ... }
  else setState('idle')
}
```
Careful stateT increments once per update. `startAttack` resets stateT. If chaining inside updateAttack, okay but stateT then 0 and attack set. Need avoid returning and physics? Fine.

Enemy combos: `startEnemyAttack(game)` picks pattern; `this.enemyPattern`, `this.enemyPatternIndex`.
When attack ends:
- If !isPlayer and enemyPatternIndex < pattern.length-1 and rng<chainChance and player alive → increment and start next after maybe 0? We can chain immediately. But perhaps fair to have small gap; each attack has recover.
- else set idle, attackCd = random.
- For player: buffered or combo window.

`performHits`:
- Get targets. For player targets = game.enemies; for enemy = [game.player].
- Hit only once each per attack.
- `if (target.canBeHitBy(this, a))`.
- `target.receiveHit(this,a,game)`.
- If any hit, `this.hitSomething=true`.
- Add slight hitstop in game.

`inHitbox(target)`:
```
const dx = (target.x - this.x) * this.facing;
const dy = Math.abs(target.y - this.y);
return dx > -6 && dx < a.range + target.w/2 && dy < a.height;
```
a.height maybe 34-44.
- Jumped over: dy = 55 > 34 → miss.

`receiveHit`:
```
if dead return;
if this.iframe>0 { 
 if (this.isPlayer && this.state==='dodge' && !this.perfectDodge) game.onPerfectDodge(...)
 else if (!this.isPlayer && this.state==='dodge') game.onEnemyDodge(this)
 return 'miss'
}
if (this.state==='parry') {
 if (!a.unblockable) {
   if (this.stateT <= this.parryWindow) { game.onParry(this, attacker); return 'parry' }
   return this.blockHit(...)
 }
}
return this.takeDamage(...)
```
- `iframe` for dodge; set to 0.22 and decrement.
- Perfect dodge should only trigger for player, with `if this.state==='dodge' && this.stateT<0.16`. Set perfectDodge flag to avoid multiple.
- For enemy dodge, game.onEnemyDodge maybe show "DODGED" but not necessary every time. Add small "MISS" text.

`takeDamage`:
```
const dir = Math.sign(this.x-attacker.x)||attacker.facing
let dmg = a.damage * (attacker.isPlayer?1:attacker.damageScale)
if (this.state==='stagger') dmg*=1.5
this.hp -= dmg
this.flash=0.12
this.invuln=0.35
this.hurtDur = a.hurt || .24
this.setState('hurt')
this.vx = dir* (a.knock||110)
if (a.launch) this.vy = -a.launch
game.onDamage(this, attacker, dmg, a)
if (this.hp<=0) this.die(game)
```
- If player gets hit, game.shake, hitstop; combo reset.
- If target is enemy: posture += a.posture*0.55; if posture>=max and not stagger => breakStagger.
- Enemy hurt state interrupts attack. Good.
- Player invuln prevents stunlock.
- `a.unblockable` is red.

`blockHit`:
```
const dmg=a.damage*0.22
hp-=dmg; posture+=a.posture*1.4; vx=dir*70; flash
game.onBlock
if enemy && posture>=max -> stagger
else setState('block'?) maybe keep parry? Set state 'parry' continue? If late parry, remains parry; add pushback. Better setState('block',0.12) and hurt? 
```
- Add 'block' state with duration .16, friction. Player can act after. Draw shield.
- If player blocks, chip health; no stagger.
- For enemy block, if posture breaks -> stagger.
- If hp<=0 die.

`parry` events:
`game.onParry(defender, attacker)`:
- attacker.stagger(.65); attacker.vx = dir*160? Defender parry pushes attacker.
- attacker.posture += 35 for enemies; if >= max break.
- Defender flash cyan; parry cooldown maybe; defender.heal(3)? Let's give player +2 HP on parry, capped. That rewards.
- slowmo(0.3) if defender player; hitstop .08; shake 7.
- score += 150 * combo? Track parries. Text "PARRY".
- Sound clang.
- Camera zoom? no.
- combo: player combo++ on parry? Score. Add `game.combo` increments and `bestCombo`.
- For enemy parry, player staggered .35, no damage; text "DEFLECTED", sound enemy parry, camera shake.
- If attacker is boss, stagger shorter maybe .45; still.

`stagger(dur)`:
- set state 'stagger', stateT 0, duration stored, vx knock.
- If player? Enemy parries player -> player hurt? We'll use stagger for player too (deflected) with duration .35 and no damage. But player posture not visible. Fine.
- For boss guard break maybe.

`die`:
- hp=0; state dead; stateT=0; vx=knock; vy=-60? fall; 
