Now charge particles in Game update. Add after player update and enemy update maybe. Better helper method. In update loop after enemies updated:
```
this.updateChargeFx(worldDt);
```
Add method near updateEffects / spawn. Need avoid adding particles when hitstop. Update only during normal world update. Implement:

```
updateChargeFx(dt) {
  for (const f of [this.player, ...this.enemies]) {
    if (!f.alive || f.state!=='attack' || !f.attack || !f.attack.charged || f.stateT >= f.attack.windup) { f.chargeFx=0; continue; }
    f.chargeFx = (f.chargeFx||0) - dt;
    if (f.chargeFx > 0) continue;
    f.chargeFx = 0.055;
    const k = clamp(f.stateT / Math.max(.001,f.attack.windup),0,1);
    const a = rnd(0,TAU), r = rnd(10,18+k*12);
    this.addParticle({
      type:'spark', x:f.x + Math.cos(a)*r, y:f.y-30+Math.sin(a)*r*0.65,
      vx: -Math.cos(a)*rnd(18,42), vy: -Math.sin(a)*rnd(12,30)-10,
      grav:-12, drag:1.2, life:rnd(.18,.38), max:.38, size:1,
      color: f.isPlayer ? '#ffe6a4' : '#ffc27a',
    });
  }
}
```
Use `alive` getter. If f.attack.charged but in active, reset. Good.

Add call after enemy update; before resolve collisions.

